 * Every Xero and LHDN call this application made, request and response.
 *
 * Exists so a consuming project can render the traffic on ITS OWN dashboard.
 * This package ships no viewer for it -- the schema is the interface, and the
 * models beside it are the supported way in.
 *
 * TWO WARNINGS, both of which have cost someone a weekend somewhere:
 *
 *   THIS IS NOT A LEDGER. The row is written AFTER the response, so a worker
 *   killed mid-call leaves no row at all. "Did that invoice reach Xero?" is
 *   answered by xero_write_records, which is inserted BEFORE the request
 *   precisely so it survives that. Never answer it from here.
 *
 *   BODIES ARE REDACTED ON THE WAY IN, never on the way out. Bank details and
 *   credentials are removed before the insert, because a raw row reaches the
 *   binary log, the nightly backup, the read replica and every SELECT * in a
